cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the Bend Emblem, no permission or attribution is required. If you want to cite where these files came from, cite it as below."
title: The Bend Emblem — vector masters and open-source package
version: "v1.1"
date-released: "2026-09-10"
type: dataset
url: https://bendemblem.com/download/
repository-code: https://github.com/grysngrhm-tech/bend-emblem
# No `license:` field, and no `identifiers:` block. Both wait on the
# provenance review recorded in the BendEmblem.com repository
# (docs/research/licensing.md). Naming a licence here before that review has
# an outcome would create exactly the ambiguity the review exists to avoid,
# around a mark whose own publisher gave it to the town in 1922. No Zenodo
# DOI is minted for the same reason.
abstract: >-
  The historic Bend Emblem: a solid disc with BEND knocked out, published in
  the Bend Bulletin on 3 July 1912 by the Bend Park Company and worn by
  members of the Bend Emblem Club, who swore in 1913 to keep wearing it
  "until Bend has a population of one hundred thousand". This repository
  holds five vector masters and the complete package built from them — SVG,
  PNG at five sizes, PDF, EPS, DXF, favicons and web assets — so that anyone
  can put the emblem on a window, a shirt, a sticker, a sign or a machine.
  The files are a modern reconstruction, not a scan of the original artwork;
  masters/RECONSTRUCTION.md records exactly what is known about their
  derivation and what is not.
keywords:
  - Bend
  - Oregon
  - civic emblem
  - local history
  - public history
  - open source brand
  - vector
  - SVG
authors:
